 "debrief": "In Tacitus’s account, Otho stayed behind at Brixellum and pushed his generals to fight. His army came on in a marching column among the vineyards along the Via Postumia. A false rumour that the Vitellians had deserted made Otho’s men cheer and stop fighting. The Batavians destroyed Otho’s gladiators by the Po. Otho’s army was beaten, and Otho killed himself to end the civil war. The other choices are what-ifs.",
